---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { ShieldCheck, ArrowRight } from "lucide-react";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — Pod Studio"
  description="Read Pod Studio's transparent, 100% client-side privacy policy. Learn how our tools process calculations, artwork, and notes locally in your browser."
>
  <div class="w-full py-10 sm:py-16">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 space-y-8">
      <div class="space-y-3">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded-full border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800 bg-white dark:bg-[#0a0a0a] text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 font-mono text-[11px]">
          <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-500"></span>
          PRIVACY-FIRST ARCHITECTURE
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">
          Privacy Policy
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xs text-neutral-500 font-mono">
          Last updated: November 1, 2026 • Effective Date: November 1, 2026
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-xl border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800 bg-white dark:bg-[#0a0a0a] space-y-6 text-xs sm:text-sm text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed">
        <section class="space-y-2">
          <h2 class="text-sm sm:text-base font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">1. The Client-Side Model</h2>
          <p>
            Pod Studio (&ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo;, or &ldquo;our&rdquo;) provides free online utilities for podcast creators at <strong class="text-neutral-900 dark:text-white font-mono">podstudiotools.com</strong>.
          </p>
          <p>
            Our core architecture is built on a simple promise: <strong class="text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">your creative ideas and audio assets belong to you</strong>. Unlike cloud-based AI tools that upload and store your text, outlines, and audio transcripts on remote databases for training or profiling, Pod Studio executes calculations and formatting <strong class="text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">100% locally inside your web browser memory</strong>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-2">
          <h2 class="text-sm sm:text-base font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">2. Data Handling by Tool Category</h2>
          <div class="space-y-2">
            <div class="p-3.5 rounded-lg border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800 bg-neutral-50 dark:bg-black space-y-1">
              <span class="font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white block text-xs">Cover Art Preview &amp; Image Testing</span>
              <p class="text-neutral-500 text-xs">
                When you drop or select a podcast cover art image in the Cover Art Preview tool, the file is loaded into your browser&apos;s volatile memory via the HTML5 FileReader API. The image data is never uploaded, stored, or transmitted over any network connection. When you close or refresh the page, the image memory is purged automatically.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="p-3.5 rounded-lg border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800 bg-neutral-50 dark:bg-black space-y-1">
              <span class="font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white block text-xs">Episode Titles, Show Notes, Scripts &amp; Hooks</span>
              <p class="text-neutral-500 text-xs">
                All text generation and string formatting formulas execute deterministically on your client device using client-side JavaScript. No episode topics, guest names, or proprietary notes are logged, recorded, or sent to server endpoints.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-2">
          <h2 class="text-sm sm:text-base font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">3. Third-Party Tracking &amp; Analytics</h2>
          <p>
            We do not use aggressive third-party trackers, cross-site profiling scripts, or advertising pixels. Your interactions with our calculators remain private.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-2 pt-4 border-t border-neutral-100 dark:border-neutral-900">
          <h2 class="text-sm sm:text-base font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">4. Contact &amp; Questions</h2>
          <p>
            If you have questions regarding our privacy architecture, email us at <a href="mailto:hello@podstudiotools.com" class="text-[#0070f3] hover:underline font-mono">hello@podstudiotools.com</a> or visit our <a href="/contact" class="text-[#0070f3] hover:underline">Contact page</a>.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>

      <div class="text-center">
        <a
          href="/tools"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-5 py-2.5 rounded-full bg-[#171717] dark:bg-white text-white dark:text-black font-medium text-xs hover:opacity-90 transition-opacity"
        >
          Explore All 18 Tools <ArrowRight className="w-3.5 h-3.5" />
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
